A thought:

If a spell were to be remembered forever after, many people object to unlimited
use of "identify".  What if identify either destroyed the object while 
identifying it, or there was a chance of destruction?  This distruction 
could occur either before or after you discovered what it was.

Also, if spells are to remain in memory, either overconfidence or inexperience
should cause varible results.  After all, you are not reading it word for word from a magic book.  If you slip on a word, you could cast an entirely 
different spell, perhaps not often of a benificial nature.  Most likely you 
wouldn't remember where you skrewed up, so wouldn't actually learn the 
wanted/unwanted spell.  Or maybe large expendatures of power could attract 
demons?

